ast sits slightly below the combined baseline.", "watch": "The House GOP TV campaign against Gillen and any movement on tax or immigration issues on Long Island could tighten the race if it lands with suburban voters.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Laura Gillen (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Laura Gillen, a first-term Democratic incumbent, seeks re-election in a Nassau County district that leans Democratic by about two points. She faces Republican Jeanine Driscoll, who won her primary in June and has raised roughly $265,000, a fraction of Gillen's $5.1 million haul. A Libertarian candidate is also on the ballot.\n\nNo public general-election polling is available, so the picture rests on fundamentals and expert judgment. Most raters place the race at Likely Democratic or safer, though Inside Elections calls it Tilt Democratic and Sabato's Crystal Ball says Lean Democratic. Prediction markets price Gillen's chances around 91 to 95 percent. House Republicans have reserved television ads against her, and Driscoll has attacked her tax votes, but Gillen has emphasized federal funding for local fire departments, police, and water infrastructure.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9622, "margin": 11.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9401, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9422, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9272, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9344, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9323, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9557, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9565, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9413, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9576, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9503, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9565, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9405